# Sample golden set for `svod-engine eval <config.json> <golden.jsonl>`.
#
# One JSON object per line: "q" is a query as you would type it, "gains" maps a note path
# (relative to the vault root) to how relevant that note is for the query:
#   3 = the note that answers the question
#   2 = a strong, useful match
#   1 = related, fine to see in the list
#   0 = not relevant (same as leaving the path out)
# Every query needs at least one note with a gain above 0.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are skipped. A '# Section ...' line starts a group:
# every query below it is also reported on its own, so a weak subset (another language, a
# harder kind of question) is not hidden by the average.
#
# Copy this file next to your config, replace the paths with notes from your own vault, and
# keep it out of any public repository if the queries say something private.

# Section 1 - en
{"q": "how do I deploy the engine", "gains": {"ops/deploy.md": 3, "ops/launchd.md": 1}}
{"q": "where do the nightly backups go", "gains": {"ops/backup.md": 3}}
{"q": "decision about the search ranking", "gains": {"decisions/search-ranking.md": 3, "notes/search-ideas.md": 1}}

# Section 2 - bg
{"q": "как се деплойва engine-ът", "gains": {"ops/deploy.md": 3, "ops/launchd.md": 1}}
{"q": "къде отиват нощните бекъпи", "gains": {"ops/backup.md": 3}}
